# shir_nodes/clone_deep.node — CloneDeep: a DEEP COPY of any store value
# (`x.clone()` under the Rust Clone bound).
#
# GENERIC. Soundness: Rust's clone NEVER aliases the original (that is
# the contract of the Clone bound), so an independent deep copy is the
# exact semantics for every store-representable value (strings, numbers,
# arrays, records). An IDENTITY lowering would be the aliasing bug the
# value-store model must not guess.
# Backends: JS structuredClone(value) (Node >=17 global); other backends
# may refuse until they pick their deep-copy primitive (Perl would be
# Storable::dclone).

node CloneDeep
tag "CloneDeep"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field value: expr
# Spec: TextOps#clone_deep_sound (docs/fm/TextOps/ShIR_TextOps_Strings.thy, section
# "CountedFor, Spread, AddressOf/Deref, CloneDeep: value-level laws"). Proved: the copy's
# VALUE equals the source's (`hread b (clone_cell a b h) = hread a h`), and mutating the
# copy through a different address leaves the source's value unchanged — the independence
# law a shallow copy breaks by aliasing the two addresses.
#
# MISSING MODEL, named rather than assumed: the address being DIFFERENT is a side
# condition, not a theorem here. Minting a fresh address belongs to the allocator, and
# proving "shares no path" for a NESTED structure needs an alias/heap-identity model with
# per-cell provenance that this theory does not have; sharing inside the copy, cycle
# handling and the GC/lifetime story are therefore unstated, not silently claimed.
# Spec: TextOps#clone_deep_sound (docs/fm/TextOps/ShIR_TextOps_Strings.thy, section
# "CountedFor, Spread, AddressOf/Deref, CloneDeep: value-level laws"). Proved: the copy's
# VALUE equals the source's (`hread b (clone_cell a b h) = hread a h`), and mutating the
# copy through a different address leaves the source's value unchanged — the independence
# law a shallow copy breaks by aliasing the two addresses.
#
# OPEN REFINEMENT, named: "the copy shares no path with the source" for a NESTED structure
# needs an alias/heap-identity model with per-cell provenance, and minting the fresh address
# is the allocator's job — here the addresses differ as a SIDE CONDITION. Sharing inside the
# copy, cycles, and the GC/lifetime story are therefore unstated, not silently claimed.
spec: TextOps#clone_deep_sound
